.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH completions 1  "completions " 
.SH NAME
completions \- Print shell completions to stdout (bash|zsh|fish|elvish|powershell). The trailing field flags are parsed by wrex itself and are not in the completion set; spell them via `wrex fields`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcompletions\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print shell completions to stdout (bash|zsh|fish|elvish|powershell). The trailing field flags are parsed by wrex itself and are not in the completion set; spell them via `wrex fields`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
Shell to emit completions for (bash|zsh|fish|elvish|powershell)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
